<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 137 0 R
/E (TRAVLR Mobile Apps is a work-based group project developed during my internship at PT TRAVLR GUIDES INDONESIA, where I worked with one fellow UI/UX Designer Intern. The project aimed to transform an existing web-based travel platform into a redesigned mobile-first experience, as research showed that most users accessed the platform through mobile devices. The app helps users discover destinations, explore accommodations, manage bookings, and plan their trips more intuitively.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [21]
>>
endobj
298 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 137 0 R
/E (My role involved analyzing user behavior, demographic insights, internal data, and existing product flows to identify user needs and design opportunities. I contributed to creating competitor analysis, user flows, wireframes, high-fidelity designs, prototypes, design iterations, and the Travlr AI feature innovation concept for personalized travel discovery. The design was validated through Maze usability testing with 23 respondents across 14 testing blocks, helping the team refine the experience based on real feedback. Through this project, I learned how to work in a real industry environment, collaborate with cross-functional teams, and balance user needs, business goals, and technical considerations.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
